{
  "recordedAt": "2026-10-23T17:52:50.800Z",
  "notes": [
    "Before bundles were retained from the checkout at the start of this further optimization pass. They already include the earlier durability, point-access, tuple-COW and index optimizations. No branch/worktree changes were used.",
    "Before/after reports use the same 33 current workload definitions: three warmups, nine samples, setup/verification/cleanup outside timings. Snapshot samples each capture and encode ten fresh 10,000-row snapshots; operations=100000 counts encoded rows, not snapshots.",
    "Before is diagnostic without --check because it intentionally exceeds the new allocation/schema-copy limits. All correctness checks still ran. After passed --check, including deterministic allocation/work limits and WASM reference comparisons.",
    "Paired diagnostics use both retained bundles in one process, five warmups and 31 samples per implementation, alternating before/after order every iteration. Both live fixtures are validated; insert setup/verification/cleanup are excluded from timings and fixtures are recreated each iteration. These diagnostics are separate from the CI gate.",
    "Wall-clock measurements remain sensitive to load, JIT and GC. The paired timing report follows completion of repository checks and CPU profiling. Diagnostic profiles include process setup and verification as well as the three-second worker loop.",
    "Browser first/reloaded reports use real WebKit IndexedDB/localStorage. The emulated IndexedDB timing in the automated report measures adapter CPU/correctness, not physical IO latency.",
    "encodedCopyBytes counts copies of the codec output, not total adapter memory traffic or storage writes. MemoryDurabilityBackend still constructs a complete image; actual IndexedDB commits only changed pages. Sparse controller copies drop from 8 MiB to 16 KiB, unchanged flushes copy none, and dense/initial/resized writes use one full-image copy.",
    "Paired diagnostics predate the final adapter-only IndexedDB compaction. None of the nine paired memory/encoding/collection workloads uses IndexedDB. Bundle hashes identify the final standalone reports. Final 33-workload reports and real browser reports include compaction.",
    "Dense IndexedDB probe observes actual objectStore.put input buffers: 64 pages of a 1 MiB image submit 64 MiB of backing buffers before, 1 MiB after. Native WebKit reads back exactly 64 pages with 1 MiB of total backing buffers on both page loads. No physical disk-throughput claim is inferred from emulated timings."
  ],
